---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const INBOX_EMAIL = "kaelnventures@gmail.com";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="SignOff – SMS Approvals for Trade Contractors"
  description="Get customer approval for extra work by SMS in seconds. Audit log included. Free trial coming soon. Beta testers welcome."
  hideBanner={true}
  hideAiHelp={true}
  hideFooter={true}
>
  <article class="signoff-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">SignOff</p>
    <h1>Get extra-work approval by text. Keep the job moving.</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      SignOff is a simple SMS tool for independent mechanics and specialty trade contractors.
      When you find unexpected work on site, send a one-tap approval link. The customer approves or declines from their phone. You get a clear record.
    </p>

    <p class="trial-note">
      <strong>Free trial coming soon.</strong> Beta testers are encouraged to submit their info below.
    </p>

    <div class="cta-row">
      <a href="#waitlist" class="btn-primary">Join the beta</a>
    </div>

    <section class="stats">
      <div class="stat">
        <strong>~98%</strong>
        <span>of SMS messages are read, most within minutes</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <strong>No app</strong>
        <span>Customer taps a link. No download, no account.</span>
      </div>
      <div class="stat">
        <strong>Audit trail</strong>
        <span>Every view, approve, and decline is logged with time and IP.</span>
      </div>
    </section>

    <h2>What it does</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>You create a job and request approval for the extra amount and description.</li>
      <li>The customer receives an SMS with a secure link.</li>
      <li>They approve or decline in one tap.</li>
      <li>You get notified and can see the full timeline on your dashboard.</li>
      <li>Optional payment request after approval.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Works with the systems you already use</h2>
    <p>
      SignOff includes an MCP connection so you (or your software) can send customer and job data straight in. No duplicate entry.
      Create jobs and request approvals from another tool, then pull the approval status and full audit trail back into that system when you need it.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions contractors ask</h2>
    <div class="qa">
      <h3>How do I get a customer to approve extra work without a phone call?</h3>
      <p>Send the SMS link while you are still on site. Most people open texts immediately. The approval is recorded before you leave.</p>

      <h3>What if the customer says they never approved it?</h3>
      <p>You have a timestamped record of the link they opened and the decision they made, including IP and device details.</p>

      <h3>Does the customer need to download anything?</h3>
      <p>No. The link opens in their phone browser. They tap Approve or Decline and are done.</p>

      <h3>Can I send from my own number?</h3>
      <p>Yes. The current setup can send from a phone you control, so the text comes from a real number instead of a short code.</p>

      <h3>Can I feed customer data from another system?</h3>
      <p>Yes. The MCP connection lets you push jobs and customers in and pull approvals and the audit log back out. No retyping.</p>

      <h3>What trades is this for?</h3>
      <p>Mobile mechanics, HVAC, plumbing, electrical, and other on-site trades where extra work is common and verbal approval creates disputes later.</p>
    </div>

    <section id="waitlist" class="waitlist">
      <h2>Join the beta</h2>
      <p>Free trial coming soon. Beta testers: tell us a little about your business and we will reach out when a spot opens.</p>

      <form
        id="waitlist-form"
        method="POST"
        action={`https://formsubmit.co/${INBOX_EMAIL}`}
      >
        <input type="hidden" name="_subject" value="SignOff beta / waitlist" />
        <input type="hidden" name="_captcha" value="false" />
        <input type="hidden" name="_template" value="table" />
        <input type="hidden" name="_next" value="https://askbeforeyoubook.com/signoff-thanks/" />
        <input type="text" name="_honey" style="display:none" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off" />

        <label for="name">Your name</label>
        <input type="text" id="name" name="name" required placeholder="Alex Rivera" />

        <label for="business">Business name</label>
        <input type="text" id="business" name="business" required placeholder="Rivera Mobile Mechanics" />

        <label for="trade">Trade / specialty</label>
        <input type="text" id="trade" name="trade" required placeholder="Mobile mechanic, HVAC, plumbing…" />

        <label for="phone">Phone</label>
        <input type="tel" id="phone" name="phone" required placeholder="+15551234567" />

        <label for="email">Email</label>
        <input type="email" id="email" name="email" required placeholder="you@example.com" />

        <label for="city">City / service area</label>
        <input type="text" id="city" name="city" placeholder="Austin, TX" />

        <label for="note">Anything else? (optional)</label>
        <textarea id="note" name="note" rows="3" placeholder="How often do you need extra-work approval?"></textarea>

        <button type="submit">Request beta access</button>
      </form>

      <p class="fine">We only use this to contact you about SignOff. No spam.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .signoff-page {
    max-width: 680px;
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding: 1rem 0 3rem;
  }
  .eyebrow {
    color: #64748b;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    letter-spacing: 0.04em;
    text-transform: uppercase;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: 2rem;
    line-height: 1.2;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  .lead {
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: #334155;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .trial-note {
    background: #eff6ff;
    border: 1px solid #bfdbfe;
    border-radius: 8px;
    padding: 0.75rem 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1.5rem;
    color: #1e3a8a;
  }
  .cta-row {
    margin-bottom: 2rem;
  }
  .btn-primary {
    display: inline-block;
    background: #1d4ed8;
    color: white;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.4rem;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-weight: 600;
    text-decoration: none;
  }
  .btn-primary:hover {
    background: #1e40af;
  }
  .stats {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(auto-fit, minmax(160px, 1fr));
    gap: 1rem;
    margin: 2rem 0;
  }
  .stat {
    background: #f8fafc;
    border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    border-radius: 10px;
    padding: 1rem;
  }
  .stat strong {
    display: block;
    font-size: 1.35rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.25rem;
  }
  .stat span {
    font-size: 0.9rem;
    color: #475569;
  }
  h2 {
    margin-top: 2rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.75rem;
  }
  ul {
    padding-left: 1.2rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  li {
    margin-bottom: 0.4rem;
  }
  .qa h3 {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.35rem;
  }
  .qa p {
    color: #334155;
    margin-bottom: 0.5rem;
  }
  .waitlist {
    margin-top: 2.5rem;
    padding: 1.5rem;
    background: #f8fafc;
    border: 1px solid #e2e8f0;
    border-radius: 12px;
  }
  .waitlist label {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: 0.9rem;
    margin-bottom: 0.3rem;
  }
  .waitlist input,
  .waitlist textarea {
    width: 100%;
    padding: 0.7rem 0.85rem;
    border: 1px solid #cbd5e1;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-family: inherit;
  }
  .waitlist button {
    margin-top: 1.25rem;
    padding: 0.85rem 1.4rem;
    background: #1d4ed8;
    color: white;
    border: none;
    border-radius: 8px;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 1rem;
    cursor: pointer;
  }
  .waitlist button:hover {
    background: #1e40af;
  }
  .fine {
    margin-top: 1rem;
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    color: #64748b;
  }
</style>
